Part 02: The Purpose of a Personal Website
In a world dominated by social media algorithms, short video clips, and fast AI content, building and maintaining your own personal website offers genuine value for self-growth and personal preservation. Having a space of your own gives you total creative control to design, update, and shape your site on your own terms. As you continuously work on it, you gain real technical proficiency instead of relying on restrictive third-party apps.
 
Additionally, learning HTML and CSS to build webpages by hand gives you a clear understanding of the specific roles each language plays—with HTML handling the structure and CSS directing the visual styling. While automated site builders, templates, and chatbots offer quick shortcuts, learning to code from scratch gives you real problem-solving skills, total flexibility over your content, and the practical confidence to troubleshoot errors and customize your site exactly how you want.
